# Lab 06 – Introduction to Modbus

## Overview

This lab introduces the **Modbus industrial communication protocol** and demonstrates how Modbus/TCP communication can be observed and analyzed in a controlled ICS/SCADA laboratory environment.

The practical exercise used **FUXA HMI**, **OpenPLC Runtime**, and **Wireshark** to observe communication between the SCADA system and PLC.

> **Note:** This work was performed in an authorized ICDFA training environment for educational and cybersecurity training purposes.

---

## Lab Objectives

The main objectives of this lab were to:

- Understand the basic operation of the Modbus protocol.
- Identify common Modbus function codes.
- Observe Modbus/TCP communication between a SCADA system and PLC.
- Capture Modbus traffic using Wireshark.
- Identify Modbus requests and responses.
- Analyze Function Code 4 (Read Input Registers).
- Identify the register associated with the tank-level value.
- Understand the security implications of unprotected industrial protocol traffic.

---

## Laboratory Environment

| Component | IP Address | Role |
|---|---|---|
| OpenPLC | `192.168.1.10` | PLC / Modbus TCP Server |
| SCADA / FUXA | `192.168.1.20` | HMI / Modbus TCP Client |
| Kali Linux | `192.168.1.30` | Network Analysis / Wireshark |

The Modbus/TCP communication was observed on the isolated `ICDFA-Lab` network.

### Communication Flow

```text
FUXA / SCADA
192.168.1.20
      |
      |  Modbus/TCP
      |  TCP Port 502
      |
      v
OpenPLC
192.168.1.10
      ^
      |
   Wireshark
   Kali Linux
192.168.1.30
